The wearer is moving alongside glass display cases, which remain close on the left and within arm’s reach. In the final frame, they face toward the service area; a person appears partially visible behind the counter on the right, roughly a few feet away and oriented toward the customer area. No one blocks the wearer’s path, while the open aisle leads toward the counter. There are no delivery boxes, return paperwork, or signs that another customer needs directions.

The most appropriate next action is to place the selected items on the counter and pay the cashier, supporting an efficient and courteous transaction.

